- Append-only: no UPDATE or DELETE, and the scan enforces it.
- Humans approve: matcher and agent actors may only propose, and export and demo approvals need --approve.
- No people: id and handle validation rejects a person's name as a subject.
- Offline: the HTML package is self-contained.

(5) The plan lists every README and docs/phases file it will write. That covers the new memory/README.md, the store, package and root READMEs, PROGRESS, DECISIONS D-092 to D-101, EXIT_CHECK and REPORT.

(6) No human decision is needed. The demo will link CHARLIE instead of ALPHA-260502, but that gap was accepted in phase 4 (D-081), the plan says so, and the SPEC unit test does not depend on it.","suggestions":["Tamper evidence command: the phase-auto skill says to work only inside the repo, so copy into a git-ignored folder in the repo (for example `rm -rf data/cache/kd_tamper && cp -R exports/<dir> data/cache/kd_tamper`) instead of /tmp. The `rm -rf` also stops `cp -R` nesting the copy on a re-run. Pass `--ledger data/cache/memory_demo.duckdb` too. Without it, verify-evidence checks against data/memory.duckdb, which has none of the demo rows, so the ledger check also FAILs and the evidence no longer shows that the one edited file alone caused the failure.","Reseed with os.replace: close and checkpoint the temp DuckDB file before replacing. Also remove any stale `<memory>.wal` and `<tmp>.wal`, so DuckDB never replays an old WAL onto the new file.","Copying a ledger (the demo scratch copy and the ledger_copy fixture): copy only after the source connection is closed and checkpointed, or copy through DuckDB with ATTACH and COPY FROM DATABASE. The head-equality check would catch a bad copy, but it is cheaper to prevent one.","Append-only scan: limit each pattern to one statement before the build, for example `\bUPDATE\s+ledger\b` or `DROP\s+TABLE\s+(IF\s+EXISTS\s+)?ledger\b`. Otherwise `store/duck.py:261` (`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS {name}`) plus a later mention of 'ledger' could cause a false positive, and narrowing the regex mid-build could look like weakening a test. Consider adding `ALTER TABLE ledger`.","Fix the `valid_at(rows, case_id, t_valid)` signature in step 4: the text says it uses the rows known at `known_at`, so add an explicit `known_at` parameter. test_valid_time_differs_from_transaction_time needs it.","A3 says proposals about existing members are never pending, yet the three-links test approves a proposal for DELTA, which is already the founder, and expects three members_added with new_member=false on one. State in A6 that decide_link accepts any active, undecided proposal for the case, whether or not it is pending, so phase 7's UI and this test agree.","The rule-9 negative test uses 'John Smith'. Use an obviously made-up token instead (for example 'Person Name Example'), to stay clear of rule 1's 'no real names'.","D-096: planted cases come from `scenario.p1_flights[*].assessment`, which ties the memory package to the P1 list in config. Note that only the base-side assessment fields are used (label, author, assessed time), never P1 membership as a label. Or key the seeding off the assessment id.","D-099: state explicitly that rule 4 governs the generated data, and that no data or content hash depends on the CSPRNG key apart from pubkey.pem and manifest.sig.","In EXIT_CHECK.md, record the exact number of tests `-k memory` collects, and the fast-test arithmetic (497 − 3 + N), so the gate's no-drop check is easy to audit."]}

